# Modus Web Components + Next.js Best Practices

## 🎯 Overview

This rule captures proven best practices for creating shareable, maintainable Modus Web Components in Next.js applications. These patterns ensure consistency, performance, and developer experience across projects.

## 🏗️ Component Architecture Principles

### ✅ Single Configurable Component Pattern

**ALWAYS** create one flexible component instead of multiple specific components:

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Single configurable component
interface ModusButtonProps {
  color?: "primary" | "secondary" | "tertiary" | "warning" | "danger";
  variant?: "filled" | "outlined" | "borderless";
  size?: "xs" | "sm" | "md" | "lg";
  shape?: "rectangle" | "square" | "circle";
  disabled?: boolean;
  fullWidth?: boolean;
  icon?: string;
  iconPosition?: "left" | "right" | "only";
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onButtonClick?: () => void;
  ariaLabel?: string;
}

export default function ModusButton({
  color = "primary",
  variant = "filled",
  size = "md",
  shape = "rectangle",
  disabled = false,
  fullWidth = false,
  icon,
  iconPosition = "left",
  children,
  onButtonClick,
  ariaLabel,
}: ModusButtonProps) {
  return (
    <ModusWcButton
      color={color}
      variant={variant}
      size={size}
      shape={shape}
      disabled={disabled}
      fullWidth={fullWidth}
      onButtonClick={onButtonClick}
      aria-label={ariaLabel}
    >
      {icon && iconPosition === "left" && (
        <i className="modus-icons" style={{ marginRight: "8px" }}>
          {icon}
        </i>
      )}
      {children}
      {icon && iconPosition === "right" && (
        <i className="modus-icons" style={{ marginLeft: "8px" }}>
          {icon}
        </i>
      )}
      {icon && iconPosition === "only" && <i className="modus-icons">{icon}</i>}
    </ModusWcButton>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG: Multiple specific components
// ModusButtonDemo.tsx
// ModusButtonSecondary.tsx
// ModusButtonWarning.tsx
// ModusButtonDanger.tsx
```

### 🎨 Styling Best Practices

#### ✅ Use Figma-Inspired Design System with Modus Colors (Recommended)

**ALWAYS** use a comprehensive design system that maps Figma variables to Modus's 9-color system:

#### 🎯 Important: Modus Web Components vs Custom UI Colors

**CRITICAL DISTINCTION**: There are two different color systems at play:

1. **Modus Web Components** (e.g., `<modus-wc-button>`) have their own predefined colors:

   - `color="primary"` → Uses `--modus-wc-color-info` (blue)
   - `color="secondary"` → Uses `--modus-wc-color-warning` (yellow)
   - `color="tertiary"` → Uses `--modus-wc-color-base-300` (gray)
   - `color="warning"` → Uses `--modus-wc-color-warning` (yellow)
   - `color="danger"` → Uses `--modus-wc-color-error` (red)

2. **Custom UI Elements** (non-Modus components) use our design system colors:
   - `--primary` → `--modus-wc-color-info` (blue)
   - `--secondary` → `--modus-wc-color-base-300` (gray) ← **NOT yellow!**
   - `--accent` → `--modus-wc-color-info` (blue)
   - `--destructive` → `--modus-wc-color-error` (red)

**Why this matters:**

- **Modus Web Components**: Use their built-in color props (`color="secondary"` = yellow)
- **Custom UI**: Use design system colors (`bg-secondary` = gray, not yellow)
- **Consistency**: Yellow is too bright for secondary UI elements, gray is more appropriate

**Examples:**

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Modus Web Component with built-in colors
<modus-wc-button color="secondary">Button</modus-wc-button>
// This will be YELLOW (--modus-wc-color-warning)

// ✅ CORRECT: Custom UI element with design system colors
<div className="bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground">Custom Card</div>
// This will be GRAY (--modus-wc-color-base-300)

// ❌ WRONG: Don't mix the systems
<div className="bg-secondary">Custom Card</div>
<modus-wc-button color="secondary">Button</modus-wc-button>
// These will have different colors (gray vs yellow) - inconsistent!
```

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT: Using Tailwind classes with design system colors
export default function MyComponent() {
  return (
    <div className="bg-card border border-border p-4 rounded-lg">
      <div className="text-4xl font-semibold text-foreground">Title</div>
      <p className="text-lg text-foreground opacity-80">Description</p>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```tsx
// ❌ WRONG: Semantic HTML elements override Tailwind classes
<h1 className="text-4xl font-semibold">Title</h1> // Won't work!

// ❌ WRONG: Inline styles override Tailwind classes
<div
  className="text-4xl md:text-5xl" // This won't work!
  style={{ color: "var(--modus-wc-color-base-content)" }}
>
  Title
</div>
```

