## 🎯 Performance Benefits

### ✅ Single Component Approach

- **90% Less Code**: One component vs 4+ separate files
- **Better Bundle Size**: Smaller JavaScript payload
- **Easier Maintenance**: Single source of truth
- **Consistent Behavior**: All buttons work the same way
- **Type Safety**: One interface to maintain

### ✅ Inline Styles Approach

- **No CSS Module Overhead**: Faster compilation
- **Theme Compatibility**: Automatic theme switching
- **No Style Conflicts**: Scoped to component
- **Better Performance**: No CSS parsing overhead

## 📋 Migration Checklist

When refactoring existing components:

- [ ] ✅ **Audit Components**: Identify duplicate/specific components
- [ ] ✅ **Create Single Component**: Build flexible, configurable component
- [ ] ✅ **Update Imports**: Replace specific components with single one
- [ ] ✅ **Remove Old Files**: Delete unnecessary component files
- [ ] ✅ **Convert Styles**: Replace CSS modules with inline styles
- [ ] ✅ **Test Functionality**: Ensure all features work correctly
- [ ] ✅ **Update Documentation**: Reflect new component patterns

## 🚀 Quick Start Template

```tsx
// app/components/Modus[ComponentName].tsx
"use client";

import { ModusWc[ComponentName] } from "@trimble-oss/moduswebcomponents-react";

interface Modus[ComponentName]Props {
  // Define all possible props
  variant?: "default" | "alternative";
  size?: "sm" | "md" | "lg";
  disabled?: boolean;
  children: React.ReactNode;
  onAction?: () => void;
}

export default function Modus[ComponentName]({
  variant = "default",
  size = "md",
  disabled = false,
  children,
  onAction,
}: Modus[ComponentName]Props) {
  return (
    <ModusWc[ComponentName]
      variant={variant}
      size={size}
      disabled={disabled}
      onAction={onAction}
    >
      {children}
    </ModusWc[ComponentName]>
  );
}
```

